---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const interpretOffersResult = await interpretOffers(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const interpretNeedsResult = await interpretNeeds(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretOffersResult.accepted);
const generateReuseResult = await generateReuse(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretNeedsResult.accepted);
const assembleExchangeResult = await assembleExchange(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, generateReuseResult.accepted);
const verifyTransferResult = await verifyTransfer(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, assembleExchangeResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { interpretOffers: interpretOffersResult, interpretNeeds: interpretNeedsResult, generateReuse: generateReuseResult, assembleExchange: assembleExchangeResult, verifyTransfer: verifyTransferResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...interpretOffersResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...interpretNeedsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...generateReuseResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...assembleExchangeResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...verifyTransferResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...interpretOffersResult.checks, ...interpretNeedsResult.checks, ...generateReuseResult.checks, ...assembleExchangeResult.checks, ...verifyTransferResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A material is offered by weight but needed by volume: require density evidence before exact conversion. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require density evidence before exact conversion.) through the existing stage result for SurplusOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior SurplusOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — An offer is withdrawn after matching: invalidate dependent exchange legs before confirming them. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (invalidate dependent exchange legs before confirming them.) through the existing stage result for SurplusOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior SurplusOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — Equipment has unknown maintenance history: require qualification rather than assuming operability. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (require qualification rather than assuming operability.) through the existing stage result for SurplusOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior SurplusOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A recipient accepts only part of a lot: release remaining quantity back to availability. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (release remaining quantity back to availability.) through the existing stage result for SurplusOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior SurplusOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A creative reuse requires specialist approval: keep the match provisional until that approval exists. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (keep the match provisional until that approval exists.) through the existing stage result for SurplusOffer; preserve exact source/version and the prior SurplusOffer, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, interpretOffers: interpretOffersResult, interpretNeeds: interpretNeedsResult, generateReuse: generateReuseResult, assembleExchange: assembleExchangeResult, verifyTransfer: verifyTransferResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
